 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t one objectively “best” company, but **Luxury Property Care (LPC)** looks like a strong first call for a Fort Lauderdale rental home based on the information available: it specifically manages single-family homes locally and publishes clear pricing—**8–10% of collected rent**, plus a **one-time leasing fee of one month’s rent** when it places a tenant. It says there’s no management fee while the home is vacant and no renewal fee. Those are the company’s own claims, so verify them and ask for the full fee schedule and contract terms.\n\nBefore choosing, compare at least two proposals and ask each company about:\n- Recent owner references for single-family rentals\n- Tenant screening and eviction procedures\n- Maintenance markups, approval limits, and after-hours response\n- Leasing, renewal, cancellation, and vacancy fees\n- Who holds rent and security deposits, and how often you receive statements\n\nI’d also confirm the manager’s Florida license and read recent reviews from **property owners**, not just tenants.",
